{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:19:41Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 202, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "12-  by color.\n13-- Existing form pattern is `AddTask.jsx`: a `<form onSubmit>` wrapping an\n14-  `<input>` + submit `<button>`, client-side `.trim()` check before calling\n15:  the handler, `aria-label` on the input.\n16-- Existing per-row actions (`TaskList.jsx`) are plain-text buttons with an\n17:  `aria-label` that includes the task's title (`` `Complete ${task.title}` ``)\n18-  for screen-reader disambiguation between rows.\n19-- Existing error surface is a single global banner in `App.jsx` \u2014\n20-  `<p className=\"error\" role=\"alert\">` \u2014 fed by `run()`'s catch block.\n--\n197-  a known, pre-existing characteristic rather than a silent gap.\n198-- **Row gap**: existing `.task` `gap: 0.5rem` (8px) already satisfies\n199-  `touch-spacing` between the new buttons \u2014 no change needed.\n200:- Input `aria-label=\"Task title\"` \u2014 reuses `AddTask.jsx`'s exact label\n201-  (line 20). Fine to reuse verbatim: only one row is ever in edit mode at a\n202-  time (assumption 2), so there's never a duplicate-label ambiguity for\n203-  screen readers at any given moment.\n204:- `Edit`/`Save`/`Cancel` buttons get `aria-label`s that include the task\n205-  title, matching the existing `Complete ${task.title}` / `Delete\n206-  ${task.title}` convention:\n207:  - `aria-label={`Edit ${task.title}`}`\n208:  - `aria-label={`Save new title for ${task.title}`}`\n209:  - `aria-label={`Cancel editing ${task.title}`}`\n210-\n211-## Exact code changes\n212-", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_017f7WgLn91HzUVTzPrAeXV6", "session_id": "a37ae859-7a64-42e7-931c-2398d2ba4b7e"}}
